# Versioned releases

After a **usable** host or APK change, pack and commit **by default**. Do not wait to be asked. Do not skip packaging. Do not make a second empty commit if the packer already committed.

- Both host and APK changed: `python pack_release.py --bump -m "why this version is usable"`
- Host only: `python build_host_exe.py --bump -m "why"`
- APK only: `python build_apk.py --bump -m "why"`
- Either single packer accepts `--no-commit` so a combined pack can commit once
- Shared helper: `release_git.py`

- Keep `VERSION.txt` as the release number (APK `versionCode` / commit title). Use `--bump` for each usable release
- Commit source, `VERSION.txt`, and `dist/LX04-PC-Bridge.apk` (current only). Host is `dist/LX04-PC-Bridge-Host/` (onedir, local only — GitHub 100MB)
- Rollback of APK is git history of that current artifact. Do **not** write `dist/LX04-PC-Bridge-Host-v*.exe` or `dist/LX04-PC-Bridge-v*.apk`
- Do **not** `git add` the host onedir, extra EXEs/APKs in `dist/`, `dist/vbcable/`, `driver/`, or `host/lx04mic/`
- VB-CABLE lives once under `host/vbcable/` (official pack). Do not duplicate it into git via `dist/`
- Commit message: `Release vN: <why this version is usable>`
- If an LX04 is on USB, install the new APK after packing (`host/安装到音箱.bat`, or `adb_usb.install_apk` with an **absolute** APK path)
- No `git push` unless the user asks
